No requirement resolves to a model node. The common reason is the ordinary one: an entry at L4 or L5 that simply declares no `@implementedBy` yet, which is legal and is what a `planned` entry looks like. The others are an entry sitting ABOVE the L4 link floor (where a claim is not permitted), a `retired` entry (where it is forbidden outright), and a claim that names a node nothing resolves — `meta verify` is what says which.
